<title>SOUTH KOREA: Hyundai Corp in $300 mln Burmese project.</title>
<headline>Hyundai Corp in $300 mln Burmese project.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hyundai Corp, a trading unit of South Korea's Hyundai Group, will take part in a $300 million Burmese project to develop an industrial estate and a port, a Hyundai Corp spokesman said on Friday.</p>
<p>The project will be financed 40 percent by the Burmese government and the rest by a consortium of Hyundai Corp and Singapore's Sinmardev International Pte Ltd. No more details were given.</p>
<p>The estate, 18 kms south of the capital Rangoon, would be developed by the year 2000. Port facilities in the estate would be completed by June 1998, he said.</p>
<p>- Seoul Newsroom 822-7275645.</p>
</text>
